\description{
Intensity-based occupancy of every modification site in every run (or sample), from a table of MS/MS-identified peptidoforms with their per-run intensities, with the censoring state of each cell.

For a site (protein, position, modification) in a run, occupancy is the summed intensity of the
quantified peptidoforms that carry the modification there, over the summed intensity of every
quantified peptidoform that covers the position - the estimator MetaMorpheus writes as
\code{IntensityOccupancy_}. Each cell keeps its state, so a censored cell is never mistaken for a 0: a
\code{"floor"} (the modified form was identified but not quantified) is low but not zero, and
\code{"not_detected"} (peptidoforms covering the site were identified in the run, quantified or not, and
none carried the modification; mzLib #1468) is a bound below what the run could detect. Neither
has a \code{fraction}.
}
\details{
mzLib always leaves out the categories \code{Common Variable} and \code{Common Fixed}, peptide-terminal
modifications and every C-terminal modification. An N-terminal modification is a site only on a
peptide that starts at residue 1, or at 2 after the initiator Met is removed.
}
\value{
An \code{mzlibr_site_occupancy}:

  - \code{records}, a data.frame with one row per (site, run) where the site was identified or
    covered, by protein, then run, then position and modification: \code{site_key},
    \code{accession:residue position:modification}, the key \code{\link{ptmqtl_pairs}} and
    \code{\link{ptmqtl_trait_effects}} use; \code{protein_accession}; \code{position}, the 1-based residue (a protein
    N-terminal modification at the residue it sits on); \code{residue}; \code{modification},
